I think you've missed the point.  A blessed scroll of identify does _not_
identify everything in your pack, it identifies "one or more items."  So,
the point is you can specify an order of importance for what you want 
identified.  As the original poster indicated, suppose you want a 
certain ring identified, and after that you might want to know what
that wand is.  If they are assigned letters such that the wand comes
_before_ the ring when you hit <RETURN>, i.e., the ring is 'R' and the 
wand is 'f', if you pass by the wand to identify the ring it won't go 
back through your inventory to let you identify the wand.  You'll just
get 'That was all.'

The importance of the original post was that if you are asked a question
'What type of things do you want to ______ (identify, drop, pick-up,
etc) (")[?!/(*) aA ?  You can enter _more_ than one type of thing.  So
if in the pile of orc stuff you want to pick up both the black knife
and the black cap, you can ask to pick-up [) instead of having
to go through the pick-up routine twice.  

Decreases keystrokes, good hint in my book.

